      "content": "That feeling of being an empty shell is a very real and agonizing part of this kind of deep loss. It sounds like your entire identity was woven into that relationship, and now the threads are gone, leaving you adrift. You don't have to find \"you\" all at once; sometimes the only thing to do is just let the current carry you for a while. Please consider reaching out to a grief counselor who can help you navigate this profound shift in your sense of self.",
